Sadly, lots of us just do not have time to sort through the bug tracker. 
Eventually, we need to decide what to do with the bug tracker. I've 
almost convinced myself that bug tracking is the job of the distro 
maintainers and each distro should develop there own process to collect 
user issues.

> Everybody, please go to http://tinyurl.com/pb9ftf from time to time and 
> see if there isn't something you want to commit.  That search result is 
> also linked from http://bugs.openembedded.net -> "Open tickets with 
> patches" link

We do seem to do a much better job with patches sent to this list. The 
patches are tracked at:

http://patchwork.openembedded.org/project/openembedded/list/

Patches that can be appliaed via git-am will get processed the fastest.

Philip

